    "https://www.queensu.ca/religion/teaching-position-available-fall-2023-rels-398897": {
      "title": "Teaching Position Available",
      "description": "Teaching Position Available - Fall 2023 - RELS 398/897 | School of Religion Skip to main content Skip to footer Sign In School of Religion Main navigation Home Undergraduate Down arrow Undergraduate Overview Degree Programs & Plans Current Course Offerings RELS Courses at a Glance RELS Courses as Electives Departmental Student Council Student Forms Quick Links FAQs Graduate Down arrow Graduate Overview MA Program Admission Requirements Application Process Funding and Awards Current Course Offerings Graduate Supervision Resources for Graduate Students Our Students People Down arrow People Overview Administration Faculty Down arrow Faculty Overview Amarnath Amarasingam Richard S. Ascough Dustin Atlas Danielle LaGrone Jennifer S. Leath Jorge Legoas P. Sharday C. Mosurinjohn Aditi Sen Tracy J. Trothen M. Shobhana Xavier Emeritus and Retired Faculty Postdoctoral Fellows Down arrow Postdoctoral Fellows Overview Teaching Fellows Down arrow Teaching Fellows Overview Research Down arrow Research Overview Faculty Publications Religion, Gender, Sexuality and Youth Down arrow Religion, Gender, Sexuality and Youth Overview Project Aims Research Team Advisory Committee Results Contact Alumni Down arrow Alumni Overview Alumni Profiles News & Events Down arrow News & Events Overview News Events Employment Opportunities Contact Teaching Position Available - Fall 2023 - RELS 398/897 May 09, 2023 RELS 398/897— Judaism in the Modern Age The School of Religion in conjunction with Jewish Studies at Queen’s University invites applications from suitably qualified candidates interested in teaching a cross-listed course in Judaism in the Modern Age (RELS 398/897). This is an on-campus, upper-level lecture course with an expected enrolment of ~35 students. The deadline to submit an application is June 2, 2023. Job Description Here Article Category Employment Opportunities News Queen's School of Religion Theological Hall, Suite 211 Kingston, ON K7L 3N6 Canada Tel: 613 533