      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Collective Agreements / LoU's / MoA's | Faculty Relations Office Skip to main content Skip to footer Sign In Faculty Relations Office Main navigation Home Queen's University Faculty Association (QUFA) Down arrow Queen's University Faculty Association (QUFA) - Overview Collective Agreements / LoU's / MoA's Professional Support Program Down arrow Fund for Scholarly Research and Creative Work and Professional Development (Adjuncts) Professional Expenses Renewal, Tenure/Continuing Appointment, Promotion (RTP) Templates Harassment by Students Conflict Resolution Services Years of Experience Guidelines Salary Statistics Down arrow 2025-26 Faculty Salary Statistics 2024-25 Faculty Salary Statistics 2023-24 Faculty Salary Statistics 2022-23 Faculty Salary Statistics 2021-22 Faculty Salary Statistics PSAC, Local 901, Unit 1 Down arrow PSAC, Local 901, Unit 1 - Overview Collective Agreements / LoUs / MoAs Resources Down arrow Resources Overview Classification of Research Fellowships and Research Assistantships Held by Graduate Students Schedule A  - Wage and Stipend Rates Templates/FAQ's PSAC, Local 901, Unit 2 Down arrow PSAC, Local 901, Unit 2 - Overview Collective Agreements / LoU's / MoA's Childcare Benefit For Post-Doctoral Fellows (PSAC, Local 901, Unit 2) 2019 Templates & Frequently Asked Questions Schedule A - University Policies and Procedures Committees Contact our Office Down arrow Contact Us - Overview Office Directory Voluntary Phased Retirement Program (VPRP) Down arrow Letter of Agreement (\"LoA\") #4 - VPRP Application Form Process & Guidelines Other Retirement Resources Qufa Collective Agreements / LoU's / MoA's Collective Agreements / LoU's / MoA's QUFA Collective Agreements 2022-2025 Queen's University - QUFA Collective Agreement - Clean Version (PDF 2430)kb 2022-26 - Queen's University - QUFA Collective Agreement -  as of March 2026 C lean Version (PDF 2MB) COVID-19 Emergency Letter of Understanding (\"LoU\") LOU re COVID-19, dated May 23, 2020: This Letter of Understanding between the University and QUFA, and associated Memoranda of Agreement in four (4) Schedules, address modifications of the Collective Agreement, most of which are temporary in duration, in the context of the COVID-19 pandemic.  Schedules A and D apply. Schedule A Schedule D Memoranda of Agreements (\"MoA's) From time to time, the Parties to the Collective Agreement, through the Joint Committee on the Administration of the Agreement (“JCAA”), agree to amend or modify the application of the Collective Agreement. The Parties’ agreement is recorded in a Memorandum of Agreement and sometimes requires amendment of provisions of the official copy of the Collective Agreement. In accordance with Article 4.3 of the Collective Agreement, the on-line, posted version is the \"official copy” of the Collective Agreement, and a link on the Faculty Relations’ website is provided to MoAs of general application concerning the Collective Agreement . MoA re QUFA and Queen's Course Delivery (2021) (PDF317KB) LoA #4 - Voluntary Phased Retirement Program (VPRP) 2022-25 (PDF 1110KB) Application form (PDF Fillable Form) as of December 7, 2023 Application Form Process & Guidelines (Jan 2024) - PDF 254) LoA re:  Recruitment and Retention (PDF 118) as of May 16, 2023 Library Letter (PDF 156) as of May 16, 2023 MoA Joint Communication re Association Grievance Regarding Term Adjuncts Performing Clinical Instruction in the School of Nursing Queen’s University and QUFA have reached an agreement regarding the compensation structure applicable to Term Adjuncts assigned to instruct or course coordinate clinical courses at the School of Nursing (the “Going Forward Framework”). The Going Forward Framework will apply going forward, covering the remainder of the current Collective Agreement and through the term of the renewed Collective Agreement. This means that this framework will apply from now until the expiry of the next Collective Agreement between QUFA and Queen’s University. The Parties’ agreement follows significant negotiation efforts respecting the compensation structure for Term Adjuncts instructing clinical courses or engaging in course coordination of clinical courses at the SON. Both parties remain committed to a productive and respectful working relationship. The full agreement can be found here. MoA Relating to the Negotiation of a Roll-Over Agreement (\"Roll-Over MoA Communication: Change in Status Regarding Endpoint Requirements for Term Adjunct Faculty Members (PDF 77KB) Dec 2025 Faculty Relations Office 74 University Avenue, Richardson Hall, Suite 153 (Lower level) Kingston, ON K7L 4N6 Canada Tel: 613.533.6000 Email: fro@queensu.ca Web Privacy Queen’s University is situated on the territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabek . © 2026 Queen’s University"
    },
