    "http://www.queensu.ca/facultyrecruitment/": {
      "title": "Immigration and Relocation Support",
      "description": "Employee Immigration and Relocation Support | Queen's University Skip to main content Skip to footer Sign In Immigration and Relocation Support Main navigation Home Immigration Down arrow Information for Employers Ontario Immigrant Nominee Program (OINP) Information for Employees and Postdoctoral Fellows Information for Visitors Social Insurance Number (SIN) Down arrow Social Insurance Number (SIN) Information for Employees Relocation Down arrow Relocation Overview Planning Your Move Housing Setting Up Your Household Health Care Child Care Schools and After School Activities Banking in Canada Taxes and Investment Considerations Settlement Services Employment for Spouses/Partners Driver's Licence and Vehicle Registration Getting Oriented to Campus Down arrow Orientation to Campus Resources for New Staff and Faculty Life in Kingston Down arrow Discover Kingston Cost of Living Location and Neighbourhoods Diversity, Faith, and Culture Accessibility Recreation, Volunteering, and the Arts Contact Welcome Home Immigration and Relocation Support Services Immigration and Relocation Support Services The Immigration and Relocation Support team advises incoming employees on their move to Kingston as they join the Queen's community. Providing immigration and relocation services demonstrates our commitment to diversity and inclusion for all. Queen’s University welcomes staff and faculty from every province and territory within Canada and around the world. Creating a diverse workforce strengthens our community and aligns with the University’s values of Truth, Responsibility, Respect, Freedom, and Wellbeing. Immigration Services Immigration Services at Queen's University provides consultation, guidance, and advice to the university community on immigration matters related to employment and to the hosting of international academics and researchers. We maintain the employer compliance regulations required by Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada (IRCC) with accuracy and transparency. Learn more about immigration support: Information for employers (inviting/hiring/rehiring a foreign national) Information for new and current employees (staff/faculty/postdoctoral fellows) Information for inviting visitors (visiting undergraduate and graduate students, professors, scholars, lecturers) Relocation Services Not sure where to start learning about your prospective new community, and how you and your family can thrive here? Relocation Services at Queen's provides personalized assistance identifying and addressing your needs before, during, or after your relocation to Queen's and Kingston. Immigration and Relocation Support Richardson Hall 74 University Avenue Kingston, ON K7L 3N6 Canada Footer Office of the Provost and Vice-Principal (Academic) Office of the Vice-Principal (Culture, Equity, and Inclusion) Footer Menu 2 Accessibility Hub Human Resources Campus Map Contact Web Privacy Queen’s University is situated on the territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabek . © 2026 Queen’s University"
    },
